I won't giveyou any spoilers, but here's some help with the interface:
-Look in options. Down near the bottom there's a pickup_burden and
pickup_types. You can set autopickup to ask you whether to pick up
something or not when it would make you burdened, and you can tell it
to only pick up certaim things. so you could've started by witching it
to only pick up weapons, and put the limit on unburdened. I susally
have it set to unburdened and $"=/? (money, amulet, ring, wand and
scroll, since these are pretty light). You can set these in the menu
once in your game, and it will save it for you (you'll have to set it
again for every new character)
-Another of the options is autopickup_exceptions, which allows you to
say specific things you want to always or never autopickup. This
setting is not saved with the game, so you have to set it when you
load a game or set it in the init file. So you can set it to always
pickup all arrows by adding a rule that says "<* arrow*" (without the
quotes), or pickup your BDD dagggers with "<* named BDD". When I
started using that I was resetting it on every load, so I had it say
"<* named Q" and then I'd name anything in my quiver Q. TYhat way I
could walk and pickup my arrows and daggers without picking up other
peoples'. In your batle you could've told it to always pick up daggers
and arrows, and, to avoid picking up any other weapons or anything,
change your types to "_" (You can't set pickup_types to none, but "_",
iron chains, are very rare and don't weight much)

If you like these options you can change the default by running
notepad, going into your nethack directory and finding a file named
nethack.nh (or a file named nethack of type "NH file") and drag it
onto the notepad. The file has nice comments on all the thigns you can
change. lines starting with # are ignored, so you can leave yourself
notes. Mine includes the lines:

OPTIONS=autopickup,pickup_types:$"=/?
autopickup_exception="<* named Q"
autopickup_exception=">* named NO"

(hmm, I guess I never changed it to unencumbered, I'll have to fix
that)
Anyway, with those your exceptions get restored every time you restore
a save file or start a new character. Change them to what you like.
The second exception says that never pickup anything named "NO", even
if it matches the pickup_types or any other exception. There's a
reason I use it, but it would be spoilery to tell you.


